{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>תום</b> — Integrity of heart and uprightness of deeds will guard him, so that he does not walk in a crooked path. It is also ready, that it will guard him from enemies; therefore after it, <b>פדה</b> — and just as he prayed that HaShem will guard him and let not his enemies rule over him, so may He redeem all Israel."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:35.423216163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}